g that's mandatory for  interns but it's a really good way to  gain an understanding of technical aws  concepts and get some hands-on  experience  [Music]  at 12 o'clock i have a virtual catch-up  with an aws solutions architect  i typically try to schedule around two  to three calls each week with people  outside  my team and i find it to be a really  good way to learn about the different  roles and teams in the company  as well as get some useful career advice  from people from all sorts of  backgrounds  now it's time for lunch and today we're  heading to xanax square to  try out a new place called toasty smith  [Music]  after lunch we tune into a virtual  fireside chat with the amazon leader  as summer interns we get invited to a  lot of these online events and q and a  panels  so it's a really good way to hear from  some more senior people in the business  and ask any questions that we have  around three o'clock now and i'm taking  a break by getting a drink and chatting  with a few people in the kitchen  [Music]  what did you do today we went for a  good stroll a good stroll down darling  hour  but yeah for the next two hours i sit  down to do some work  and since it's the second week of my new  role i'm mainly going through some  training modules to get an understanding  of my intern project and learn more  about what the team does  after work we head to a dinner and  drinks event and get to know some  interns from other teams  and this basically wraps up my work day  now i head home spend some time with my  family help out with some chores  and get ready for bed  [Music]  if you enjoyed seeing a day in my life  as an amazon intern please give this  video a like and subscribe for more tech  and student advice videos  let me know in the comments below if you  have any questions bye for now
 

